\description{
Quantifies the environmental niche overlap between every pair of taxa in the
geographical/environmental matrix produced by \code{\link[=geo_matrix_setting]{geo_matrix_setting()}}. Climate
variables (and, when available, edaphic variables) at the occurrence points
are combined in a single principal component analysis (PCA), and niche
overlap is measured in the plane of the first two axes with Schoener's D,
following the PCA-env framework implemented in \pkg{ecospat}. For each pair,
niche equivalency and niche similarity are tested by permutation, and niche
dynamics indices (expansion, stability and unfilling) are computed.

Environmental variables are taken automatically from the \code{"env_cols"}
attribute of \code{geodata}, so climate-only and climate + edaphic matrices are
both handled without further arguments.
}
\details{
\strong{Input.} \code{geodata} must be the data frame returned by
\code{\link[=geo_matrix_setting]{geo_matrix_setting()}}, carrying the \code{"env_cols"} attribute. It must contain
the column \code{taxon} and the environmental columns listed in
\code{attr(geodata, "env_cols")}. The climate block (\code{"clim"}, which includes
\code{"elevation"}) is always used; the edaphic block (\code{"edaphic"}) is added when
present. All taxa in \code{geodata} are compared; to restrict the analysis, use
\code{species_selected} in \code{\link[=geo_matrix_setting]{geo_matrix_setting()}}.

\strong{Environmental space.} The workflow is:
\enumerate{
\item Environmental variables are converted to numeric and records with
any missing value are removed (at least 20 complete records are
required).
\item Variables with zero variance are dropped.
\item Highly collinear variables (|r| > \code{cor_cutoff}) are removed with
\code{\link[caret:findCorrelation]{caret::findCorrelation()}}. The variables removed are documented in
\code{Removed_correlated_variables.xlsx}.
\item A single PCA (centred and scaled) is fitted to the remaining
variables. The pooled records of all taxa define the environmental space
("background") in which every pairwise comparison is made, so overlap
values are comparable across pairs.
}

The niche analyses use the first two principal components (PC1 and PC2).
\code{var_threshold} does not change which axes are used: it defines the
cumulative-variance line on the scree plot and the number of axes reported
in the progress messages as needed to reach that threshold.

\strong{Niche overlap.} For every pair of taxa with at least \code{min_occ}
records each, an occurrence density grid of \code{grid_size} x \code{grid_size} cells
is built for each taxon with \code{\link[ecospat:ecospat.grid.clim.dyn]{ecospat::ecospat.grid.clim.dyn()}}; Schoener's
D is computed with \code{\link[ecospat:ecospat.niche.overlap]{ecospat::ecospat.niche.overlap()}} (D ranges from 0, no
overlap, to 1, identical niches); and the following are estimated with
\code{iterations} permutations:

\itemize{
\item the \emph{equivalency test}
(\code{\link[ecospat:ecospat.niche.equivalency.test]{ecospat::ecospat.niche.equivalency.test()}}), which asks whether the
niches of the two taxa are identical;
\item the \emph{similarity test}
(\code{\link[ecospat:ecospat.niche.similarity.test]{ecospat::ecospat.niche.similarity.test()}}, \code{rand.type = 2}), which asks
whether the niches are more (or less) similar than expected by chance
given the environmental space available.
}

Niche dynamics indices are computed with
\code{\link[ecospat:ecospat.niche.dyn.index]{ecospat::ecospat.niche.dyn.index()}} (\code{intersection = 0.1}): \code{expansion},
\code{stability} and \code{unfilling}, taken from the weighted index
(\code{dynamic.index.w}). Tests are significant when p < \code{alpha}. Fewer than 999
permutations triggers a warning, as they are generally discouraged for
publication. #' The random seed (\code{seed}) is set at the start of each pair for
reproducibility. Permutation results obtained in parallel
(\code{n_cores > 1}) are not guaranteed to be reproducible, because the seed
is not propagated to the workers; use \code{n_cores = 1} for exact
reproducibility.

A pair that fails at any step produces a warning and is skipped, so one
problematic pair does not stop the whole run.

